#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:91
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A model in prose is a proposal; a model in the declaration is a model. Ship a reader in the same change — everything here that was only documentation went inert within weeks."
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:82
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A naming question. The BA owns the domain vocabulary; the agent does not guess, which is CRDM's own rule for phase 1 and applies here with more force."
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:56
#. Diagram label
msgid "Agent"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "An operational question, asked of the people who run the process because they know where the exceptions are."
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:67
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answers the operational half the BA cannot — not what a thing is but how many of it there really is — because that is knowable only to the people who run the process day to day. It is also the step this process's STRICT policy exists for: skipped under time pressure, a model looks finished without it, which is exactly how a hole where the exceptions live would ship unnoticed."
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:51
#. Diagram label
msgid "BA / Feature Requestor"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:85
#. Diagram label
msgid "Confirm the cardinalities"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:81
#. Diagram label
msgid "Confirm the entities are the ones meant"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Confirms naming only — are these the entities meant — and stops there: Lane_Stakeholders asks the separate, operational question about cardinality next, and the two are kept apart on purpose, because collapsing them into one review is how a wrong cardinality ships invisibly."
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:40
#. Diagram label
msgid "CRDM data model"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:38
#. Diagram label
msgid "CRDM data model — entities, relations, cardinalities"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:90
#. Diagram label
msgid "Declare the model where a tool can read it"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Does the actual modelling — entities, relations, and the declaration that makes the model machine-readable rather than prose — and absorbs the entire cost of a revise: the gate loops back to A_Entities whichever confirmation failed, BA's or the stakeholders', so this lane cannot assume a cardinality objection leaves its entities untouched."
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:41
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Draft the data model from the BPA and the requirements, have the BA confirm the entities and the stakeholders confirm the cardinalities, and loop until both. A requirement the model cannot express is a finding, not a modelling failure: it means the requirement is about something nobody has named."
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:89
#. Diagram label
msgid "Entities recognised and every cardinality answered?"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every verb in the BPA whose object is a candidate entity, and every noun in a requirement. An entity with no identifier is an attribute of something else — that test is decisive and belongs to the technique skill."
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:73
#. Diagram label
msgid "Identify entities from the BPA and requirements"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:94
#. Diagram label
msgid "Model declared"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:77
#. Diagram label
msgid "Relations and cardinalities, both ways"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:72
#. Diagram label
msgid "Requirements agreed"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:100
#. Diagram label
msgid "revise"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:66
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stakeholders"
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:78
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Stated in both directions, because \"one attestation per report\" and \"one report per attestation\" are different claims and a model with only the first cannot say whether a re-signature is an update or a second row."
msgstr ""

#: methodologies/crdm/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn:101
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
